Technology), employment type (Full-time), location (San Francisco, CA), salary ($140k - $180k), posted date (Jan 15), and skills (React, TypeScript, CSS, Node.js).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Filtering by Technology industry: 2 jobs. Adding San Francisco location filter: 1 job. Adding Full-time employment type: still 1 job matching all criteria. Clicking \\\"Clear filters\\\" restored all filters to default and list to full 8 jobs. Filters work individually and in combination, with immediate result updates.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Keyword search tested with: \\\"Frontend\\\" (job title) = 1 result, \\\"TechCorp\\\" (company name) = 2 results, \\\"React\\\" (skill) = 1 result, \\\"react\\\" (lowercase skill) = 1 result. All searches immediately updated result count. Search is case-insensitive and matches titles, companies, and skills.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Application submitted with: name (John Smith), valid email (john.smith@email.com), optional phone (555-0123), and message. Success notification displayed: \\\"Application submitted! Your application for Marketing Manager at BrandForward Agency has been sent.\\\" Form fields cleared after submission.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-18\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No edit feature found for job listings\", \"actual\": \"Employer dashboard shows only two controls per job: toggle-applications and delete-job. No edit button, link, or option is available to modify job details. Job detail page navigation not available from dashboard.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-9\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Invalid field not identified to user\", \"actual\": \"Browser's HTML5 validation silently prevents form submission with invalid email (\\\"invalid-email\\\" without '@'), but no visual error message or indication is displayed to the user identifying which field is invalid or what the error is. Email field validity shows false with message \\\"Please include an '@' in the email address\\\", but this is not shown to the user.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-10\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Invalid salary range accepted without validation\", \"actual\": \"Job posted successfully with minimum salary (100000) greater than maximum salary (50000). No validation error or feedback was displayed to the user. Job appears on dashboard with ID job-1787751510945 and is available for job seekers.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Duplicate application accepted instead of rejected\", \"actual\": \"Second application for Marketing Manager job was submitted using the same email address (john.smith@email.com) as the first application. Both applications are now visible in the employer dashboard: app-1787751535238 (new message) and app-1787751374679 (original message). Expected: duplicate application should have been rejected.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Application submission produces success notification \\\"Application submitted! Your application for Marketing Manager at BrandForward Agency has been sent.\\\" Applications appear in employer dashboard under the matching job, displaying applicant name (John Smith), email (john.smith@email.com), and message. Each application appears as a distinct record with unique ID.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Search for \\\"NonexistentSkill123\\\" immediately updated result count from \\\"Showing 9 jobs\\\" to \\\"Showing 0 jobs\\\" and displayed \\\"No jobs found\\\" message. Previous tests confirmed that filtering by industry/location/type also immediately refreshes results and count. Clearing filters restores full list. All changes take effect immediately.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"New data not persisted after page reload\", \"actual\": \"After page reload: (1) QA Test Job posted during testing (job-1787751510945) is no longer in job seeker listing (9 jobs before reload → 8 after). (2) Applications submitted during testing disappeared from Marketing Manager job (showed 2 applications before → 0 after reload). (3) Total application count reset from 5 to 3. Only pre-existing baseline data persisted; newly created jobs and applications lost.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Each job card in the listing displays: title (Senior Frontend Developer), industry (Technology), employment type (Full-time), company (TechCorp Solutions), location (San Francisco, CA), salary range ($140k - $180k), posting date (Jan 15), and required skills (React, TypeScript, etc. shown truncated). Example: 'Technology Full-time Senior Frontend Developer TechCorp Solutions San Francisco, CA $140k - $180k Jan 15 React TypeScrip…'\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Job details page for Product Designer displays: title (Product Designer), company (TechCorp Solutions), industry (Design), employment type (Remote), location (Remote), salary ($100k - $140k), posting date (Jan 18), full description section, and required skills (Figma, UI/UX, Prototyping, User Research).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-17\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Phone number and submission date not displayed\", \"actual\": \"Application details shown for app-3 (Product Designer): name (James Wilson), email (james.w@email.com), and message displayed. Missing fields: phone number (not displayed even though optional field exists) and submission date (completely absent). Employer cannot view complete application record.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Newly posted QA Test Job (during test session) displayed as 'Yesterday' in job listing, indicating application calculates and displays relative dates for recent postings. Existing baseline jobs show absolute dates (Jan 15, Jan 18, etc.) as they are older postings. Application supports both relative and absolute date formatting based on recency.\"}]}"
